infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Acquisition timeout: fail fast vs pile up
  desc Same starved pool — bound the wait to a few hundred ms, or let every waiter hold a thread for 30 s
  compares
    - label Tuned 250 ms - 2 s: fail fast
      children
        - label Frees the upstream thread
          desc Errors in a few hundred ms, releasing the web-server worker to shed load or trip a breaker
        - label Rides normal micro-bursts
          desc Long enough to clear a 60 ms blip, short enough to give up on real starvation
        - label Preserves capacity
          desc Cheap immediate failures instead of a slow-motion collapse
    - label Default 30 s: pile up
      children
        - label Each waiter pins a thread for 30 s
          desc A web-server worker, socket, and request memory held for the whole wait
        - label Thread pool fills with waiters
          desc Hundreds of doomed requests queue; the tier stops accepting connections
        - label Slow DB becomes a full outage
          desc Thread starvation — a healthy web tier taken down by a merely slow database
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f43f5e
